 "transcript": {
  "answer": "**Victoria has the higher unemployment rate.** In September 2026, the latest month available, the seasonally adjusted rates were:\n\n- **Victoria:** 5.05%\n- **NSW:** 4.71%\n- **Gap:** about 0.35 percentage points\n\nThe gap has narrowed. In August 2026 Victoria was at 5.17% and NSW at 4.35%, a gap of about 0.8 points. NSW rose by about 0.35 points in September while Victoria fell by about 0.11.\n\nVictoria has been above NSW in every month since January 2026, when the two were almost level (4.25% vs 4.15%). Monthly state figures are volatile, so the 0.35-point gap is small enough to be partly survey noise.",
